@echo off
rem ---------------------------------------------------------------------
rem DO NOT EDIT THIS FILE WHILE IT IS RUNNING. NOT EVEN A COMMENT.
rem
rem cmd.exe reads a batch file INCREMENTALLY, BY BYTE OFFSET, as it executes
rem it. Changing the file's length mid-run moves everything after the cursor,
rem and execution resumes at an offset that no longer means what it meant.
rem
rem That cost INFRA-VIEWER-001 a four-hour qualification that had PASSED: two
rem minutes in, a comment was reworded; four hours later, when qualify.cmd
rem returned, cmd.exe resumed at a stale offset and called it a SECOND time,
rem truncating qualification-times.txt and overwriting three of debug-ext's
rem logs. The run had already printed "every stage exited 0" and the evidence
rem for it was gone.
rem
rem EVERY LINE OF THIS FILE BEGINS WITH rem, set, call, echo, setlocal,
rem endlocal OR @echo, AND THAT IS CHECKED BEFORE THE RUN.
rem ---------------------------------------------------------------------
rem
rem P17-CMD-001 COMMANDS / UNDO / REDO (ADR-047). The exact invocation,
rem recorded so the run is reproducible rather than described.
rem
rem qualify.cmd is byte-identical to the one P16-SIZE-001 settled on and every
rem milestone since has used, TWENTY-SEVEN in a row counting this one.
rem
rem   qualify.cmd          git hash-object d313a64070718c44fae290ac042fe259d1a03c8b
rem                        sha1sum         244b38de8feac0475af7cdc56ba9415d27d8dd29
rem   verify-harness.cmd   git hash-object 11855b8ff891093b021d1e0351761283d0eedd24
rem                        sha1sum         afd0197d4f4726db7f533c2f27f4f6e069ba83c6
rem
rem BOTH FORMS ARE RECORDED because they differ and a hash without its
rem algorithm cannot be checked: .gitattributes sets `*.cmd text eol=crlf`, so
rem git stores LF while the working tree is CRLF.
rem
rem CMAKE_BUILD_PARALLEL_LEVEL=6, carried for the reason INFRA-VIEWER-001
rem recorded: 16 logical cores let `cmake --build` run 18 compiles at once, and
rem a CLEAN build of over 600 template-heavy translation units exhausted the
rem commit charge. Capping parallelism weakens nothing -- same sources, same
rem flags, -Werror included. ctest stays at -j 8.
rem
rem WHAT THE AUDIT FOUND, AND WHY THIS MILESTONE IS SMALL. Four of the five
rem capabilities the brief asks for already existed. `Command`'s own contract
rem already stated the three guarantees this milestone is about: a failed
rem execute leaves the document unchanged, undo exactly reverts, and redo
rem reproduces the state execute produced INCLUDING THE SAME IDs.
rem StructuralAnalysis IS a DocumentObject, so AddObjectCommand already creates
rem and deletes one correctly. Document::modifyObject already validates through
rem setDefinition BEFORE assigning. And result invalidation is already the
rem object's REVISION.
rem
rem SO THIS RUN ADDS NO COMMAND FRAMEWORK, NO INVALIDATION MECHANISM AND NO
rem IDENTITY TYPE. Three questions the brief asked to be decided were already
rem decided by the project -- load order is the user's and preserved, an
rem analysis edit stales the result but not the mesh, and a no-op edit succeeds
rem without invalidating but is still recorded -- and following the project
rem rather than inventing answers is what the audit was for.
rem
rem WHAT CHANGED SINCE e795acb.
rem
rem   NEW          include/bettercad/structural/StructuralCommands.hpp
rem                src/structural/StructuralCommands.cpp
rem                               Eight commands. Two wrap AddObjectCommand and
rem                               DeleteObjectCommand; one base implements
rem                               execute/undo/redo once and seven subclasses
rem                               each override a single edit(before).
rem                tests/structural/StructuralCommandTests.cpp
rem                tests/compile_fail/StructuralCommandMisuse.cpp
rem
rem   MODIFIED     include/bettercad/structural/StructuralAnalysisObject.hpp
rem                               A QUALIFIED P17-DATA TYPE. The definition
rem                               gained `SolverSettings solver`.
rem                include/bettercad/structural/StructuralData.hpp
rem                src/structural/StructuralData.cpp
rem                include/bettercad/structural/StructuralSolve.hpp
rem                src/structural/StructuralSolve.cpp
rem                               SolverAlgorithm, SolverSettings and
rem                               validate(SolverSettings) MOVED here from
rem                               StructuralSolve.hpp.
rem                include/bettercad/structural/StructuralLoad.hpp
rem                src/structural/StructuralLoad.cpp
rem                               validate(const StructuralLoad&) exposed.
rem                include/bettercad/structural/StructuralValidation.hpp
rem                src/structural/StructuralValidation.cpp
rem                               solveStructuralAnalysis READS THE SETTINGS
rem                               FROM THE DOCUMENT and lost its parameter.
rem                tests/structural/StructuralDataTests.cpp
rem                               the permitted-definition MIRROR extended.
rem                tests/structural/StructuralValidationTests.cpp
rem                               its solve() installs the settings first.
rem
rem THREE PREDECESSORS ARE REQUALIFIED BY THIS RUN, and the debt is named
rem rather than assumed away: P17-DATA-001 (the definition gained a field),
rem P17-SOLVE-001 (SolverSettings moved and the solve entry changed) and
rem P17-VALID-001 (solveStructuralAnalysis is its entry point). P17-LOAD-001 is
rem requalified too, for validate(const StructuralLoad&).
rem
rem WHY THE SOLVER SETTINGS BECAME CANONICAL. The definition deliberately
rem omitted them and said why: "an empty std::vector<Setting> here would be a
rem placeholder for a type that does not exist". SolverSettings EXISTS NOW --
rem P17-SOLVE-001 created it, with its own validate -- so the reason for the
rem omission is gone rather than overruled. And the field had to exist for a
rem command to edit it: settings that live only as an argument to the solve
rem cannot be undone, redone or persisted, so a settings command would have had
rem nothing to mutate.
rem
rem THE TYPE WAS MOVED so a command header reaches the definition without also
rem reaching GlobalStructuralSystem, ConstraintSet or the Tet4 element matrix.
rem Source-compatible: StructuralSolve.hpp already reached StructuralData.hpp
rem transitively through StructuralDof.hpp.
rem
rem ONE DECLARED EXCEPTION TO THE NO-MESH-IDENTITY RULE, and the qualified
rem evidence decided it rather than the brief. A NodalForceLoad names a NodeId:
rem P17-LOAD-001 calls that "MESH-LOCAL BY DECLARATION, and that is a decision
rem rather than an oversight", the payload carries the MeshStamp it belongs to,
rem it is refused against any other mesh, and it exists for fixtures. So a
rem command that adds one carries that handle as part of a canonical record
rem that declares its own mesh binding. Forbidding it would leave a qualified
rem canonical load form with no undoable editing path. What IS forbidden, and
rem probed, is a NodeId or ElementId as a command's TARGET and every species of
rem derived solver state.
rem
rem COMPILE-FAIL: 16 cases, 16 expected failures, 0 unexpected passes, plus a
rem CONTROL target that must compile so every failure is attributable. One case
rem proved more than it was written to prove: the expected diagnostic was a
rem refused conversion and the measured one is "StructuralResult is not a member
rem of bettercad::structural", because the result header is not reachable from a
rem command translation unit at all. The case FAILED until the claim was
rem corrected, which is the right way round.
rem
rem MUTATION: 16 probe runs over 13 distinct mutations. THREE REAL TEST GAPS
rem were found and closed, and each is recorded with why nothing caught it:
rem   C8/C8b  an edit that erased and appended lost the record's POSITION, and
rem           every edit case used a single load so reordering was invisible
rem   C3      a command whose apply() FAILED still recorded a before-state and
rem           became undoable. Reachable only through
rem           SetStructuralAnalysisDefinitionCommand, whose edit validates
rem           nothing -- for the other seven commands apply cannot fail after
rem           edit succeeded, so the mutation sits in an unreachable path there
rem One equivalent mutant is kept and documented: removing the settings
rem validator from SetSolverSettingsCommand changes nothing, because
rem validate(definition) checks the solver settings itself. That asymmetry --
rem validate(definition) checks the mesh and the solver but NOT the loads or
rem restraints -- is what makes the load and restraint validators load-bearing
rem and this one redundant, and it was measured rather than argued.
rem
rem What IS in the repeat set, and why. THE FILTER IS UNCHANGED:
rem `unit\.Structural` already covers unit.StructuralCommand as a substring, and
rem `architecture` covers the new structural-to-core command edge. The SELECTED
rem COUNT IS RECORDED BY THIS RUN rather than predicted here -- a figure nobody
rem has measured does not belong in the evidence for a run.
rem
rem compile_fail is excluded from the REPEAT for the reason the previous
rem fourteen milestones recorded: each case is a real COMPILATION, so repeating
rem one measures the compiler's determinism and not BetterCAD's. They still run
rem UNFILTERED in all three presets.
rem
rem QUALIFY_REPEAT is expanded as !REPEAT! inside qualify.cmd, never %REPEAT%:
rem a %VAR% holding | ( or ) is substituted when the for-block is PARSED and
rem closes the block early, killing the run after every preset has passed.
setlocal
set "BETTERCAD_BUILD_ROOT=C:/Users/uqhas/AppData/Local/bc-build"
set "CMAKE_BUILD_PARALLEL_LEVEL=6"
set "QUALIFY_PRESETS=debug-ext release-ext debug-shared-ext"
set "QUALIFY_REPEAT_PRESETS=release-ext debug-ext"
set "QUALIFY_REPEAT=architecture|unit\.Structural|unit\.Quality|unit\.MeshDofMap|unit\.ConstraintSet|unit\.FreeEquationMap|unit\.Tet4Element|unit\.Mesh|unit\.Volume|unit\.Tet|unit\.Siz|unit\.Id|unit\.ReferenceModel|unit\.Analytic|unit\.View|refmod\.|gui\."
call "%~dp0qualify.cmd" "%~dp0."
set "RESULT=%errorlevel%"
echo qualify.cmd exit %RESULT%
endlocal & exit /b %RESULT%
